---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — motobrief"
  description="Who is behind motobrief and what this project is about."
  lang="en"
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-16">

    <header class="mb-12">
      <p
        class="text-xs text-zinc-600 mb-4"
        style="font-family: var(--font-mono);"
      >
        about the project
      </p>
      <h1
        class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-100"
        style="font-family: var(--font-sans);"
      >
        About
      </h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">

      <h2>Who I am</h2>

      <p>
        I'm Guillermo, a software developer (DAM degree) with a cybersecurity
        specialization, starting a Computer Engineering degree in September.
        I'm 22, based in Spain.
      </p>

      <p>
        My professional goal is to work in offensive security and vulnerability
        research. motobrief is the project where I turn that goal into concrete,
        documented work.
      </p>

      <h2>What motobrief is</h2>

      <p>
        motobrief is a technical security research blog focused on the digital
        ecosystem of modern motorcycles. It's not a motorcycle blog in the
        traditional sense — no reviews, no horsepower comparisons.
      </p>

      <p>What I publish here are technical analyses on:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Manufacturer apps</strong> — traffic analysis, decompilation,
          endpoint mapping, data sent to servers.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Connected devices</strong> — GPS anti-theft, Bluetooth
          trackers, OBD dongles.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Data privacy</strong> — what data apps collect, who they share
          it with, GDPR compliance.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        All research is conducted client-side only — no attacks against servers
        I don't own. Any significant finding goes through responsible disclosure.
      </p>

      <h2>Why this exists</h2>

      <p>
        The security ecosystem of modern motorcycles is largely unstudied
        compared to cars. There's serious CAN bus research for automobiles, but
        almost nothing equivalent for motorcycles. That's an interesting gap.
      </p>

      <p>
        I also want to build a technical portfolio that demonstrates what I can
        actually do, not just what I've studied.
      </p>

      <h2>Methodology & tools</h2>

      <p>
        Typical stack for analyses: <code>mitmproxy</code>, <code>jadx</code>,
        <code>apktool</code>, <code>Frida</code>, <code>Burp Suite</code>.
        Methodological reference:
        <a href="https://mas.owasp.org/MASTG/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          OWASP MASTG
        </a>.
      </p>

      <hr />

      <h2>Contact</h2>

      <p>
        Questions about an analysis, want to collaborate, or are you a
        manufacturer who wants to discuss a finding before I publish it:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Email:
          <a href="mailto:contacto@motobrief.es">contacto@motobrief.es</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          GitHub:
          <a href="https://github.com/Guilleee50" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            github.com/Guilleee50
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        PGP accepted for responsible disclosure. Key available on request.
      </p>

    </div>

  </article>
</BaseLayout>
